WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.414
Dorothy followed the Yellow Brick Road all afternoon, and then she wondered where she would sleep for the night.

2
00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:25.074
Not far ahead she saw a small Munchkin village, but all the houses seemed empty.

3
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:29.339
When she came to the last and biggest house in the village, she understood why.

4
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.339
Everyone in the village was there.

5
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.405
All the Munchkins knew who Dorothy was.

6
00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:41.264
She was famous, and Boq, the host, was very happy to have her as a guest.

7
00:00:41.265 --> 00:00:44.039
"You killed the Wicked Witch of the East.

8
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.491
You must be a powerful witch," Boq said to Dorothy.

9
00:00:49.492 --> 00:00:56.698
"I am not a witch," replied Dorothy. "I am an ordinary girl."

10
00:00:56.699 --> 00:01:03.983
"Girl or witch," said Boq, "you can stay at my house."

11
00:01:03.984 --> 00:01:08.970
In the morning Dorothy said good-bye and continued down the Yellow Brick Road.

12
00:01:08.971 --> 00:01:12.211
She hadn't walked far when she came to a cornfield.

13
00:01:12.212 --> 00:01:15.246
In the cornfield was a scarecrow.

14
00:01:15.247 --> 00:01:21.233
As Dorothy looked at the scarecrow, she thought she saw it blink its eyes.

15
00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:27.498
"Impossible," thought Dorothy. Then the scarecrow smiled and nodded its head.

16
00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:31.233
Curious, Dorothy went over to the scarecrow.

17
00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:34.435
"Good day," said the Scarecrow.

18
00:01:34.436 --> 00:01:37.296
"Did you speak?" asked Dorothy.

19
00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:41.687
"Yes," answered the Scarecrow. "How are you?"

20
00:01:41.688 --> 00:01:46.446
"I'm fine," replied Dorothy. "And you?"

21
00:01:46.447 --> 00:01:53.030
"I'm not well," said the Scarecrow. "I'm stuck to this pole. Can you help me?"

22
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:58.775
Straw men are very light, so Dorothy was able to easily lift him from the pole.

23
00:01:58.776 --> 00:02:03.315
"Thank you," said the Scarecrow. "I feel better now."

24
00:02:03.316 --> 00:02:06.328
"You're welcome," said Dorothy.

25
00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:11.516
"Who are you?" asked the Scarecrow. "And where are you going?"

26
00:02:11.517 --> 00:02:17.012
"My name is Dorothy, and I am going to the Emerald City to see the Wizard of Oz."

27
00:02:17.013 --> 00:02:21.752
"Where is the Emerald City, and who is Oz?" asked the Scarecrow.

28
00:02:21.753 --> 00:02:25.760
"Don't you know?" Dorothy asked in surprise.

29
00:02:25.761 --> 00:02:30.493
"No, I don't know anything," answered the Scarecrow sadly.

30
00:02:30.494 --> 00:02:36.019
"My head is made of straw, so I have no brain."

31
00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:42.306
"Oh," said Dorothy. "I'm sorry to hear that. Oz is a great wizard."

32
00:02:42.307 --> 00:02:47.157
"Do you think Oz could give me a brain?" asked the Scarecrow hopefully.

33
00:02:47.158 --> 00:02:54.487
"I don't know," said Dorothy. "But come with me and we will ask him together.

34
00:02:54.487 --> 00:02:58.614
I'm scared to go and see the Wizard alone. Are you scared?"

35
00:02:58.615 --> 00:03:02.510
"Oh, I'm not afraid," answered the Scarecrow.

36
00:03:02.511 --> 00:03:07.476
"I'll tell you a secret: there is only one thing in the world that I am afraid of—"

37
00:03:07.477 --> 00:03:11.690
"The farmer who made you?" interrupted Dorothy.

38
00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:16.778
"Oh no," said the Scarecrow. "I'm afraid of fire."

39
00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:22.437
"Let's not talk about fire and scary things," said Dorothy. "Tell me a story."

40
00:03:22.437 --> 00:03:27.881
"Me?" exclaimed the Scarecrow. "My life has been too short.

41
00:03:27.882 --> 00:03:30.497
I was made only two days ago.

42
00:03:30.498 --> 00:03:34.208
Why don't you tell me about the place you are from?"

43
00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:38.620
Dorothy told the Scarecrow about her aunt and uncle and their farm in Kansas.

44
00:03:38.621 --> 00:03:40.680
She was very sad.

45
00:03:40.681 --> 00:03:44.215
"Why are you sad?" asked the Scarecrow.

46
00:03:44.216 --> 00:03:49.192
"You said Kansas is dull and boring. Why do you want to go back?"

47
00:03:49.193 --> 00:03:55.942
"Because, my brainless friend, there is no place like home," said Dorothy, weeping.

48
00:03:55.943 --> 00:04:01.172
"Shall we spend the night over there?" asked the Scarecrow, pointing to a cottage.

49
00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:03.766
"Okay," said Dorothy.

50
00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:08.316
The next morning when Dorothy woke up, she said, "I need water."

51
00:04:08.317 --> 00:04:11.658
"Why do you need water?" asked the Scarecrow.

52
00:04:11.659 --> 00:04:17.319
"I need water to wash my face and to drink with breakfast," she replied.

53
00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.936
"Being alive sounds inconvenient," said the Scarecrow.

54
00:04:20.937 --> 00:04:25.125
"You need to sleep, wash, eat, and drink.

55
00:04:25.126 --> 00:04:29.685
But you have a brain, and I'd do anything for a brain."

56
00:04:29.686 --> 00:04:32.694
Behind the cottage they found a clear spring.

57
00:04:32.695 --> 00:04:38.006
Dorothy realized she didn't have much bread left, so she was glad her friend didn't eat.

58
00:04:38.007 --> 00:04:42.822
After breakfast Dorothy was startled to hear what sounded like a low groan.

59
00:04:42.823 --> 00:04:45.888
The noise came from the forest nearby.

60
00:04:45.889 --> 00:04:49.707
"Wh . . . what was that?" asked Dorothy fearfully.

61
00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:52.964
"I don't know," said the Scarecrow.

62
00:04:52.965 --> 00:04:57.198
"But we should go look. Someone may be hurt."

63
00:04:57.199 --> 00:05:01.847
They heard another low groan. "Look!" shouted Dorothy.

64
00:05:01.848 --> 00:05:04.275
"What's that through the trees?"

65
00:05:04.276 --> 00:05:07.833
They entered the forest and were amazed at what they saw.

66
00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:16.447
A man, made of tin and holding an ax, stood frozen, as if he was about to chop a tree.
